# 16 — unit parameters and deduced results
#
# `[]` is one parameter of type unit, so `f: [];` is called as `f ()`.
# Arity 0 has no brackets at all (see get_point in 05-point).
# An elided result is **deduced** from the body; `()` is explicit unit.
#
#   func: [];              unit parameter
#   assign_value: [int];   int parameter, deduced result
#   auto_function: [n:];   deduce both the argument and the result type

func: [];
assign_value: [int];
do_something: [];
auto_function: [n:];
